Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 18:25:24 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 085/202] [ae-patch] Give the session rail toggle its own icon
 and open the rail in every session from a new Chat settings section

The rail toggle drew a box with a divider, like the workspace panel toggle beside it; it and the phone menu item now draw Tabler list-details for both states, with open shown by the pressed state and fill.

A session that restored its open workspace panel closed the rail on windows up to about 1440 px, so the rail had to be reopened in session after session. A new preference, on by default and saved with the rail's layout, opens the rail whenever a session opens on a desktop; until the user acts in that session, a workspace, files or logs panel that cannot fit beside the rail closes instead. A panel opened by hand still swaps with the rail, and a deep link to a file keeps its panel. Settings > Chat, a new section, carries the switch.
